/-!
# Local and quotient reductions for Lemma 16.4.5

The standard setup supplies the SQTK involution centralizer, its genuine
C-component and quasisimple two-core quotient. The rank argument identifies
O_{p'}(C_G(i)) with C_K(i), so its quotient is canonically isomorphic to
C_G(i)* inside the fixed H/K. It also proves the ambient equality
O^{p'}(L C_K(i)) = L. The nontrivial centers of all the models in
A.3.18(3) exclude that entire alternative.

For the final H* assertion, the two-local N_G(T_C) is SQTK and its image
is all of H/K by Frattini's argument. This is the additional source of
an A.3.18 application; no SQTK hypothesis on H itself is assumed.

The complete alternatives of 16.4.5 are not yet asserted. Their assembly
still requires the literal universal A.3.18 interface with the actual
A.3.16 nonsplit extension carriers, and the (E2) restriction of its
projective rank-three models to characteristic two.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004),
Lemma 16.4.5, p.1184, and Notation A.3.16/Lemma A.3.18, pp.51–52.
-/
